  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l is far better than scgpt, and within that family transformer aggregation with weighted fusion is currently best (config_024: 0.725 accuracy, 0.685 F1), while avgpool weighted is close (config_045: 0.706). The main remaining uncertainty in this promising region is whether concat fusion with transformer aggregation can match or exceed weighted fusion. config_018 tests exactly this by keeping the best RNA encoder, image encoder, and aggregation while changing fusion to concat. It is the best next experiment because it is a direct, low-risk exploitation of the strongest configuration family, may reveal a higher-accuracy or cost-comparable variant, and leaves two experiments to follow up on any improvement. Expected relative cost is comparable to config_024, roughly 3.5-4.0 GPU hours, and likely similar to or slightly cheaper than the weighted-fusion variant."
}

